#---
# purpose: "a map update whose base the compiler knows is no map still compiles, and raises BadMapError when it runs, as in Elixir"
# oracle: self
# oracle.stamp: 24f9d061e64b4d8e
#---
#
# The binary is known at the update, so the update can never find a map. That
# is no compile error: the update takes its miss arm and raises when reached.
defmodule Main do
  def main() do
    v = "bin"
    %{v | a: 1}
  rescue
    e in BadMapError -> IO.puts(Exception.message(e))
  end
end

Main.main()
